# Copied by install.sh to ~/.omp/agent/config.local.yml — never committed.
# zshrc exports PI_CONFIG_FILES pointing at that copy, which omp layers as a
# CLI config overlay on top of the shared, tracked ~/.omp/agent/config.yml
# (symlinked from dotfiles' omp/agent/config.yml). The overlay is a deep
# merge of settings objects: only the keys present here override anything —
# every other setting, including untouched modelRoles/fallbackChains entries,
# still comes from the shared config.yml.
#
# This is the file a machine edits to run its own model routing — trial a
# model only it has a key for, add a fallback tier the shared config doesn't
# carry, point a role at a custom provider from
# ~/.omp/agent/models.yml.example — without touching the tracked config.yml
# that every machine shares. The tracked file carries a deliberately thin
# default (anthropic primary, cursor as the one shared fallback tier — no
# openai/openai-codex, since not every machine authenticates those); this
# file is where a machine that does adds them back in.
#
# It has to stay a valid object even with nothing overridden: omp validates
# the overlay's root as an object, and PI_CONFIG_FILES pointing at a missing
# or unparsable file is a hard startup error (not skipped like an
# unauthenticated built-in provider). The active `{}` below is what keeps a
# fresh copy inert without being empty.

{}

# ── Example: trial a model on a provider only this machine authenticates ────
# fireworks is one of omp's own built-in providers — authenticate it with
# `/login fireworks` (or a stored/env API key) and reference it directly, no
# models.yml entry needed. A genuinely custom provider (self-hosted, or a
# second identity for an account with its own subscription) does need one —
# see omp/agent/models.yml.example. Either way, comment what a role's
# override replaces so reverting is a one-line diff away.
#
# modelRoles:
#   task: fireworks/kimi-k2.7-code:medium      # was anthropic/claude-sonnet-5:low — trial
#   smol: fireworks/minimax-m2.7:low           # was anthropic/claude-haiku-4-5:low

# ── Example: add a fallback tier the shared config doesn't carry ────────────
# Whole chains replace, not merge, per role — the merge is a deep merge of
# YAML mappings, and a YAML list is a leaf value, not a mapping, so listing a
# role here replaces the shared config.yml's list for that role entirely
# rather than appending to it. This machine authenticates `openai`, so it
# puts it ahead of the shared cursor-only tier — anthropic (primary, from
# modelRoles) -> openai -> cursor:
#
# retry:
#   fallbackChains:
#     default:
#       - openai/gpt-5.6-terra:medium
#       - cursor/composer-2.5
